# Base Caddyfile merged with the docker-label config by caddy-docker-proxy
# (via CADDY_DOCKER_CADDYFILE_PATH). It supplies two things the labels can't
# express cleanly:
#
#   1. the global `order` directive that tells Caddy where the third-party
#      rate_limit handler runs in the chain, and
#   2. a reusable (ratelimit) snippet, applied to the site with a
#      `caddy.import: ratelimit` label on the django service.
#
# Rationale + the failure it guards against: docs/perf/crawler-repro.md.

{
    order rate_limit before reverse_proxy
}

# Three complementary limits, all shedding at the edge (HTTP 429 + Retry-After)
# before a request reaches Daphne or opens a Postgres connection. A request must
# pass every applicable zone; the tightest one wins. Thresholds were measured on
# beta (cpx21, same as prod) with an `ab` concurrency ramp; real legit traffic
# peaks at ~3.5 req/s (busiest minute in two weeks), so all three sit far above
# legit and below where Daphne collapses. See docs/perf/crawler-repro.md.
#
#   * per_ip     -- any single client IP. `key {remote_host}` is the real client
#                   IP (Caddy terminates TLS at the edge). 50/10s ~= 5 req/s.
#                   Defeats a single-IP flood (the 2026-07-15 crawler) and keeps
#                   one IP from eating the shared budgets below.
#   * list_views -- AGGREGATE across ALL IPs for the expensive, crawlable
#                   endpoints (list views + tournament pages incl. the slow RSS
#                   feed). `key static` = one shared bucket. 20/s ~= half their
#                   measured ~40 req/s ceiling. Defeats a *distributed* botnet
#                   crawl of these paths (the 2026-08-04 outage: ~24k IPs, <=4
#                   requests each -- every IP under the per-IP limit, yet the
#                   total still buried Daphne).
#   * whole_site -- AGGREGATE across ALL IPs and ALL paths: the catch-all
#                   backstop for a flood that pivots to some other endpoint.
#                   45/s ~= half the ~90 req/s ceiling of even a cheap request
#                   (every request pays the full middleware stack under the GIL,
#                   so the whole app caps near there).
(ratelimit) {
    rate_limit {
        zone per_ip {
            key    {remote_host}
            events 50
            window 10s
        }
        zone list_views {
            match {
                path /players/* /board/* /hand/* /tournament*
            }
            key    static
            events 20
            window 1s
        }
        zone whole_site {
            key    static
            events 45
            window 1s
        }
    }
}
